{"schemaVersion":"body.os.wger-details.v1","items":[{"id":"wger_960697af9a0e4bfda8ba989718b6b5c7","wgerId":914,"descriptionEn":"Standing in front of cable tower using a SZ Bar","descriptionZh":"","author":"novadani","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"novadani"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"novadani"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/914","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:36:23.497446+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_440cf10ceffb4b63a6e0182fe47376f6","wgerId":1709,"descriptionEn":"Stand with a good posture holding a cable in each hand opposite the machine Starting with the hands in front of your chest pull the arms out to your side into the shape of a T with the elbows nearly straight Slowly release the arms forward to the start Repeat with the arms moving into the shape of a Y Repeat with the arms in the shape of a W Repeat with the arms in the shape of an L by your side","descriptionZh":"","author":"Croak6728","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Croak6728"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Croak6728"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1709","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:36:43.128627+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_dd6e8753a574476e900ab794eb592e7b","wgerId":1290,"descriptionEn":"Hold the barbell with an overhand grip (palms facing down) approximately shoulder-width apart. Ensure your back is straight, shoulders slightly pulled back, and arms fully extended. Curl the barbell upwards towards your chest in a controlled motion, keeping your elbows close to your body. The motion should be smooth without any swinging or momentum use. Once the barbell is at chest level, pause briefly to maximize contraction in the biceps and forearms. Slowly lower the barbell back to the starting position with a controlled movement, fully extending your arms.","descriptionZh":"","author":"sTiKyt","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"sTiKyt"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"sTiKyt"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1290","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-10-24T15:58:18.626762+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_1b95d9611d5c4dedb25ec090295ffe37","wgerId":498,"descriptionEn":"Upper chest focuses exercise that also works triceps","descriptionZh":"","author":"bl0sh","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"bl0sh"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"bl0sh"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/498","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-04-15T22:23:55.328255+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_682ea312af02450a9880fea7bf8e854a","wgerId":1809,"descriptionEn":"Lie face-down on a bench with your legs hanging off the edge. Bend your hips so your thighs are vertical, bending your knees at the same time so your shins stay horizontal. Straighten out your legs so they are not bent and your toes are pointing backwards horizontally. Return to the original position, and repeat.","descriptionZh":"","author":"Croak6728","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Croak6728"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Croak6728"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1809","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-10-24T15:58:34.627219+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_616f90261a1d4ed8b068cfbb81b6a000","wgerId":999,"descriptionEn":"Starting position: Stand straight, feet hip-width apart. Steps: Step backward with one leg so it can bend comfortably to a 90 degree angle. Slowly bend both knees to form 90 degree angles. Return to the starting position. Repeat, alternating legs.","descriptionZh":"起始姿势：站直，双脚分开与臀部同宽。 步骤： 一条腿向后迈步，使膝盖能舒适地弯曲成90度角。 慢慢弯曲双膝，双膝均成 90 度角。 回到起始位置。 换腿，重复。","author":"","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseZh":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/999","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:25:05.323972+02:00","nameZhSource":"wger","nameZhModel":""},{"id":"wger_6cbdd70c06914288b58a24001384f1b3","wgerId":909,"descriptionEn":"Natural Leg Extension is alternative to Leg Extension machine with no equipment.","descriptionZh":"","author":"karly","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"karly"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"karly"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/909","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-05-11T00:02:42.126668+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_09349391375b42d5897900a5d7196a5b","wgerId":500,"descriptionEn":"Plank with stomach towards ceiling","descriptionZh":"","author":"spacetowaste","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"spacetowaste"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"spacetowaste"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/500","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:25:23.199107+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_edc44b1a35d74c37ab2005842fb40576","wgerId":913,"descriptionEn":"Sitting reverse on a Biceps Bench with a close grip","descriptionZh":"","author":"novadani","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"novadani"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"novadani"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/913","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-04-15T22:23:55.337477+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_603895ca20a04272a62b293d14220390","wgerId":1215,"descriptionEn":"Lay flat on your stomach with your arms extended in front of you on the ground as your legs are lying flat. Lift both your arms and move them to your side slowly. Then, move them back.","descriptionZh":"","author":"mike6426","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"mike6426"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"mike6426"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1215","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:50:24.710577+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_04063ba505d148b99571eae2b8edab29","wgerId":2620,"descriptionEn":"Step into the V-squat machine facing the pad, the opposite way from the regular V-squat, so that your chest rests against the pad and your shoulders sit under the shoulder pads. Place your feet on the platform about shoulder width apart and release the safety. Brace your core and lower yourself by bending your knees and pushing the hips back until your thighs are roughly parallel to the platform. Drive back up through the heels without locking out the knees. Compared to the regular V-squat, the reversed position shifts the emphasis towards the glutes and hamstrings.","descriptionZh":"","author":"aboksz","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"aboksz"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"aboksz"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/2620","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-10-13T20:51:29.303162+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_6f5d437366d14acda16fba0e636fe979","wgerId":1433,"descriptionEn":"Attach a looping resistance band to a rack below knee height Grip the other end of the band like holding a baseball bat with both hands Stretch the band facing it Start with your hands at the side of your hips, knees bent Rotate your hips while moving your hands towards over the top of your opposite shoulder Imagine the motion as striking a baseball with a bat","descriptionZh":"","author":"M9","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"M9"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"M9"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1433","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:52:37.157761+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_2acb5ba1caa342049903ff0095b032ba","wgerId":1292,"descriptionEn":"Pull-ups on the bar with your thumbs pointing outward.","descriptionZh":"","author":"clafal","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"clafal"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"clafal"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1292","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T17:29:56.048153+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_8374a85692934b90900e00c3bfe21cc4","wgerId":1014,"descriptionEn":"Starting position: Start standing up or sitting down. Turn your head to the right, around 45 degrees or just above your nipple. Place your left hand behind your back or sit on it. Take your right hand and use it to hold the back of your head. Lean your head down slightly. Steps: After assuming the starting position, press your head against your right hand with slight force. Your hand should press back with equal force, so that your head doesn't move. Hold this position.","descriptionZh":"","author":"","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1014","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:42:55.689042+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_7ea504e733104638a111054fabfd4b80","wgerId":1009,"descriptionEn":"Starting position: Sit or stand with your back straight. Steps: Tilt your head to the side. Take the hand closer to your head and use it to grab your head from the other side. Push with your hand against your head and with your head against your hand so that the forces balance out and your head stays still. Maintain this tension until the end of the exercise.","descriptionZh":"起始姿势：坐位或站位，背部挺直。 步骤： 头向一侧倾斜。 用离头较近的那只手从另一侧抓住头部。 手顶着头，头顶着手推动，使力量平衡，头部保持静止。 保持这种张力直到练习结束。","author":"","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseZh":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1009","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-04-15T22:23:56.719010+02:00","nameZhSource":"wger","nameZhModel":""},{"id":"wger_7671b16c50234663b00d86dd018e024f","wgerId":501,"descriptionEn":"Dips peformed on gymnastic rings.","descriptionZh":"","author":"Nash","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Nash"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Nash"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/501","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-04-15T22:23:55.355131+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_6c9c9d14e6bf43ed9859a689e2131fe0","wgerId":1832,"descriptionEn":"Hold yourself in a support position on gymnastic rings with arms straight at sides. Focus on keeping rings turned out slightly and maintaining hollow body position. This is an isometric hold for chest, shoulders, and triceps.","descriptionZh":"","author":"","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":""},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1832","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:55:23.725802+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_0dfe655eee2e4c49a279c672d5591613","wgerId":1485,"descriptionEn":"Set your feet below the rope and lean your upper body towards the rope. Set one foot back. Push down the rope and lean your entire body back onto the rear foot as you push down to get your hands behind your body. Don't forget to bring your chest to the front during the pushdown. As you release the rope slowly, lean your body back onto the front foot.","descriptionZh":"","author":"Moffi","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Moffi"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Moffi"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1485","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:36:34.136119+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_d5ee3b1f2879406f97a951a8b0817cd4","wgerId":1399,"descriptionEn":"Stand with your feet hip-width apart and slowly roll your upper body forward, one vertebra at a time, until your hands touch the ground or as far as you can comfortably go. Roll back up to the starting position in the same controlled manner.","descriptionZh":"","author":"captive0592","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"captive0592"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"captive0592"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1399","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-06-19T18:52:23.356662+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_752c0380a0f943328265cf503bac4703","wgerId":1954,"descriptionEn":"Roll-overs into V-sits Part of: Limber 11 Source: Joe DeFranco Prescription: 10 reps Type: dynamic","descriptionZh":"","author":"Pete-E automation","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Pete-E automation"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Pete-E automation"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1954","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-04-26T17:25:48.508820+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_af2f774c296c4d148e4afad77175ae37","wgerId":505,"descriptionEn":"Crunches on roman chair. Keep your torso straight, abs tight, and don't come up all the way vertical or lie flat to keep constant tension on your abs.","descriptionZh":"","author":"MaddieBeasley","license":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"MaddieBeasley"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":1,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 3","full_name":" Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 3","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en","author":"MaddieBeasley"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/505","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:24:57.588611+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_12a8040486844ff0a473d80b4ad8cd5e","wgerId":2639,"descriptionEn":"this is a really cool descriptions for an exercise I've created several tomes now but this thing won't save it","descriptionZh":"","author":"kbk","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"kbk"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"kbk"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/2639","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-09-16T06:52:15.633650+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_2e7ffff9e6034b2898c831d1a6ce8cd9","wgerId":507,"descriptionEn":"DL from top to pos 2: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WtWtjViRsKo","descriptionZh":"","author":"pjwirth","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"pjwirth"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"pjwirth"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/507","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-10-14T17:29:26.810573+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_148f2ffc05e2486b874f2a401337a1c6","wgerId":1634,"descriptionEn":"Set up bench in front of cable row machine. Lean over bench to do a row/pullover with rope that targets lats. See picture.","descriptionZh":"","author":"Rottekongen","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Rottekongen"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"Rottekongen"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1634","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-07-23T12:36:37.833638+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_849f2fa642f94c5990f6275c8ada6725","wgerId":1374,"descriptionEn":"Slow and Steady Not too much weight","descriptionZh":"","author":"6LXBO","license":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"6LXBO"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":2,"short_name":"CC-BY-SA 4","full_name":"Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike 4","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en","author":"6LXBO"},"translationLicenseZh":{},"sourceUrl":"https://wger.de/en/exercise/1374","sourceUpdatedAt":"2026-10-18T19:37:42.645022+02:00","nameZhSource":"search_translation","nameZhModel":"deepseek-flash"},{"id":"wger_4b7cb03707894014ab6fa451716b7538","wgerId":508,"descriptionEn":"In strength training, rowing (or a row, usually preceded by a qualifying adjective — for instance a seated row) is an exercise where the purpose is to strengthen the muscles that draw the rower's arms toward the body (latissimus dorsi) as well as those that retract the scapulae (trapezius and rhomboids) and those that support the spine (erector spinae). When done on a rowing machine, rowing also exercises muscles that extend and support the legs (quadriceps and thigh muscles). In all cases, the abdominal and lower back muscles must be used in order to support the body and prevent back injury.","descriptionZh":"","author":"BFad07","license":{"id":3,"short_name":"CC0","full_name":"Creative Commons Public Domain 1.0","url":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/","author":"BFad07"},"translationLicenseEn":{"id":3,"short_name":"CC0","full_name":"Creative Commons Public Domain 1.0","url":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/","author"